  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "must: obligation",
      "title_form": "Must: obligación",
      "title_target": "Must: obligation",
      "description_md_form": "**Must** expresa **obligación** o **necesidad** en inglés. Es un verbo modal: siempre va seguido de otro verbo en su forma base (sin *to*).\n\n- **Afirmativo**: *Subject + must + verbo base* → `We must protect the environment.`\n- **Negativo**: *Subject + must not (mustn't) + verbo base* → `You mustn't switch off the lights.`\n\n**Must** no cambia con la persona: *I must*, *she must*, *they must*. No necesita *do* para negar ni para preguntar.\n\nEn esta lección lo usamos para hablar de acciones necesarias para **proteger la naturaleza**: `We must protect the environment.`",
      "description_md_target": "**Must** expresses **obligation** or **necessity** in English. It is a modal verb: it is always followed by another verb in its base form (without *to*).\n\n- **Affirmative**: *Subject + must + base verb* → `We must protect the environment.`\n- **Negative**: *Subject + must not (mustn't) + base verb* → `You mustn't switch off the lights.`\n\n**Must** does not change with the person: *I must*, *she must*, *they must*. It does not need *do* for negatives or questions.\n\nIn this lesson we use it to talk about actions necessary to **protect nature**: `We must protect the environment.`",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + must + base verb",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "must_obligation",
        "headers": [
          "Pronombre",
          "Afirmativo",
          "Negativo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "I",
            "I must protect",
            "I must not (mustn't) protect"
          ],
          [
            "you",
            "you must protect",
            "you must not (mustn't) protect"
          ],
          [
            "he/she/it",
            "he must protect",
            "he must not (mustn't) protect"
          ],
          [
            "we",
            "we must protect",
            "we must not (mustn't) protect"
          ],
          [
            "they",
            "they must protect",
            "they must not (mustn't) protect"
          ]
        ]
      },
